{
  "title": "Infrastructure Overview",
  "tags": [
    "infrastructure",
    "prometheus",
    "kubelet",
    "node-exporter",
    "kubernetes"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Node CPU (cores)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Measured by each node's kubelet (job kubelet) from the node container's cgroup, so each line is one kind node. 1 = one CPU busy.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(node_cpu_usage_seconds_total{job=\"kubelet\"}[1m])",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{ node }}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Node Memory (working set)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Measured by each node's kubelet (job kubelet) from the node container's cgroup, so each line is one kind node. Working set: memory in use that can't be reclaimed, what the kubelet evicts on.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "node_memory_working_set_bytes{job=\"kubelet\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{ node }}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Pod CPU (cores)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "CPU of each pod, all its containers together, measured by the kubelet of its node. Per container: container_cpu_usage_seconds_total.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "rate(pod_cpu_usage_seconds_total{job=\"kubelet\"}[1m])",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{ namespace }}/{{ pod }}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "sortBy": "Last *",
          "sortDesc": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Pod Memory (working set)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Memory working set of each pod, all its containers together, measured by the kubelet of its node. Per container: container_memory_working_set_bytes.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "pod_memory_working_set_bytes{job=\"kubelet\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{ namespace }}/{{ pod }}",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "sortBy": "Last *",
          "sortDesc": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Docker Host CPU Usage",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "On kind the three nodes are containers on one kernel, the Docker host's (on macOS the Docker Desktop VM). node-exporter reads that kernel's /proc, so it sees the whole host, including every other container on it, never one node. This is the host's CPU in use, averaged over its CPUs and the three identical node-exporters.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "100 * (1 - avg(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{job=\"node-exporter\", mode=\"idle\"}[1m])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "Docker host",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Docker Host Memory Usage",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "On kind the three nodes are containers on one kernel, the Docker host's (on macOS the Docker Desktop VM). node-exporter reads that kernel's /proc, so it sees the whole host, including every other container on it, never one node. This is the host's memory in use (1 - MemAvailable / MemTotal).",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "avg(100 * (1 - node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes{job=\"node-exporter\"} / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes{job=\"node-exporter\"}))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "Docker host",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 9,
        "x": 9,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Scrape Targets Down",
      "type": "stat",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Targets whose last scrape failed. prometheus.localhost/targets says which and why; the TargetDown alert fires after a minute.",
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "count(up == 0) or vector(0)",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "down",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 0
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": ""
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "uid": "infrastructure"
}
